; A fixed BOOL literal in MEMBER position (`[v: true]` / `{k: false}`) panics generation at the
; fixed-value deserialize arm's catch-all (`generation.rs`'s `_ => unimplemented!()` — the match
; handles Uint/Nint/Text/Float; Bool has no arm). Distinct from BOTH neighboring supported shapes:
; fixed numeric/text members (`[v: 5]`, pinned by the matrix cells
; `contain.array-element.value.{number,text}`) and a fixed NULL member (`[null, uint]` — null has
; its own arm and generates fine). Also distinct from top-level `foo = true`, which is now a
; graceful rejection (see `tests/matrix_reject/prelude.true.cddl`). The matrix has no
; prelude-constant member containment cells (only `contain.choice-member.prelude.null`, the
; nullable pattern), so this hand fixture is the pin until either the panic is fixed or such
; cells land. Found incidentally during the top-level fixed-value rejection work.
arr = [v: true, x: uint]
